From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:26:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cix: drm: dptx: disable IRQ before draining hotplug work on
 teardown

trilin_dp_deinit_config() canceled dp->hpd_irq_work and dp->hpd_event_work before calling disable_irq(dp->irq). A hotplug interrupt firing in that window could re-queue either delayed work item after cancellation, leaving work running against stopped clocks or freed component state.

Disable dp->irq first (matching trilin_dp_pm_prepare()) and drain both delayed work items with disable_delayed_work_sync() so neither the ISR nor any other path can re-arm them during teardown.

Signed-off-by: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
index f471fb8..a56984c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
@@ -2788,9 +2788,9 @@ int trilin_dp_deinit_config(struct trilin_dp *dp)
 	int rc = 0;
 
 	DP_DEBUG("enter\n");
-	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dp->hpd_irq_work);
-	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dp->hpd_event_work);
 	disable_irq(dp->irq);
+	disable_delayed_work_sync(&dp->hpd_irq_work);
+	disable_delayed_work_sync(&dp->hpd_event_work);
 
 	mutex_lock(&dp->session_lock);
 	trilin_dp_aux_cleanup(dp);
-- 
